## Code Patterns

### ViewComponent (sidecar template)

`app/components/profile_card_component.rb`:

```ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

class ProfileCardComponent < ApplicationComponent
  # @param profile [Profile]
  # @param size [Symbol] :sm, :md, :lg
  def initialize(profile:, size: :md)
    @profile = profile
    @size = size
  end

  private

  attr_reader :profile, :size

  def container_classes
    base = 'rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4'
    size_class = case size
                 when :sm then 'w-48'
                 when :md then 'w-64'
                 when :lg then 'w-full max-w-md'
                 end
    "#{base} #{size_class}"
  end
end
```

`app/components/profile_card_component.html.erb`:

```erb
<article class="<%= container_classes %>" data-controller="profile-card">
  <header class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <%= image_tag profile.avatar_url, class: "w-10 h-10 rounded-full", alt: profile.name %>
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-semibold"><%= profile.name %></h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500"><%= profile.headline %></p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <% if profile.bio.present? %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-700"><%= profile.bio %></p>
  <% end %>
</article>
```

Render in a view:

```erb
<%= render(ProfileCardComponent.new(profile: @profile, size: :lg)) %>
```

### Turbo Frame

Wrap content that should be replaced independently of the rest of the page:

```erb
<%= turbo_frame_tag "profile_#{@profile.id}" do %>
  <%= render(ProfileCardComponent.new(profile: @profile)) %>
  <%= link_to "Edit", edit_profile_path(@profile) %>
<% end %>
```

The edit page renders the matching frame, and Turbo swaps it in:

```erb
<!-- app/views/profiles/edit.html.erb -->
<%= turbo_frame_tag "profile_#{@profile.id}" do %>
  <%= render "form", profile: @profile %>
<% end %>
```

### Turbo Stream

Broadcast updates from controllers or models:

```ruby
# In a controller
def create
  @comment = @post.comments.create!(comment_params)
  respond_to do |format|
    format.turbo_stream # renders create.turbo_stream.erb
    format.html { redirect_to @post }
  end
end
```

```erb
<!-- app/views/comments/create.turbo_stream.erb -->
<%= turbo_stream.append "comments", partial: "comments/comment", locals: { comment: @comment } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "new_comment_form", partial: "comments/form", locals: { comment: Comment.new } %>
```

### Stimulus Controller

`app/javascript/controllers/dropdown_controller.js`:

```js
import { Controller } from "@hotwired/stimulus"

export default class extends Controller {
  static targets = ["menu"]
  static values = { open: Boolean }

  connect() {
    this.close = this.close.bind(this)
  }

  toggle(event) {
    event.preventDefault()
    this.openValue = !this.openValue
  }

  openValueChanged(open) {
    this.menuTarget.classList.toggle("hidden", !open)
    if (open) {
      document.addEventListener("click", this.close)
    } else {
      document.removeEventListener("click", this.close)
    }
  }

  close(event) {
    if (this.element.contains(event.target)) return
    this.openValue = false
  }
}
```

Use it in HTML:

```erb
<div data-controller="dropdown" data-dropdown-open-value="false" class="relative">
  <button data-action="dropdown#toggle" class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded">
    Options
  </button>
  <div data-dropdown-target="menu" class="hidden absolute mt-2 bg-white shadow rounded">
    <%= link_to "Edit", edit_path, class: "block px-4 py-2 hover:bg-gray-100" %>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Form (Turbo-aware)

```erb
<%= form_with(model: @profile, class: "space-y-4") do |form| %>
  <% if @profile.errors.any? %>
    <div class="rounded bg-red-50 border border-red-200 p-3">
      <ul class="text-sm text-red-700">
        <% @profile.errors.full_messages.each do |msg| %>
          <li><%= msg %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :name, class: "block text-sm font-medium" %>
    <%= form.text_field :name, class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded border-gray-300" %>
  </div>

  <%= form.submit class: "px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded" %>
<% end %>
```

The controller MUST render with `status: :unprocessable_entity` on validation
failure or Turbo will not re-render the form.

## Style Rules (MANDATORY)

1. **`frozen_string_literal: true`** on every Ruby component file
2. **ApplicationComponent base** — all components inherit from it
3. **Keyword args** in `initialize`
4. **Private `attr_reader`** for instance variables
5. **No DB queries in components or helpers** — pass data in via `initialize`
6. **Sidecar templates** (`.html.erb` next to `.rb`) for components with markup
7. **`t('...')` for all user-visible strings** — never hardcode English
8. **Tailwind classes grouped** — layout → spacing → typography → color → state
9. **Stimulus controllers small and focused** — one responsibility each
10. **No inline JavaScript** — always a Stimulus controller
11. **Forms use `form_with`** (NOT `form_for` or `form_tag`)
12. **Buttons use `button_to` for state-changing actions** (proper HTTP method + CSRF)
13. **Always provide `alt` text** on images
14. **Always provide labels** on form fields (visible or `sr-only`)

## Component vs Partial — when to use which

| Use a ViewComponent when | Use a partial when |
|--------------------------|---------------------|
| The same UI appears in 3+ places | The UI is rendered once or twice |
| There is non-trivial logic to compute classes/values | The markup is straightforward |
| The component has variants (size, color, state) | No variants |
| You want unit tests on the component | Spec is covered by system spec |
| Slots are needed (header/body/footer pattern) | A flat parameter list is enough |

